reau that  does not require them to wear body worn  cameras they are not patrol officers and  therefore by policy they do not wear  body worn cameras as you're fully aware  over the last few nights we've had every  officer not only with our agency but  with partner agencies deployed as we  work through the events that are  occurring so these officers were brought  in from their normal duties to work the  streets that night we do have several  pieces of surveillance video from  various locations that we will show you  during this brief our suspects name is  Jorge Gomez Jorge is 20 was 25 years old  Hispanic male six foot 180 and he is  pictured to my left mr. Gomez was armed  with three firearms on this night the  first one was a Glock 23 40 caliber with  a carbine conversion kit you can see it  a picture to my left this is actually a  pistol that is inserted into a carbine  conversion kit that allows it to perform  like a rifle ii firearm that he was  armed with was a Glock 19  nine-millimeter handgun that was on his  holster on his side the third was a  Glock 17 nine-millimeter handgun that  was illegally concealed in a backpack  that he was wearing mr. Gomez was also  wearing a full body armor he had a  ballistics vest with ballistic plates  inserted into that vest  had mr. Gomez survived he would have  been charged with four counts of assault  with a deadly weapon on a protected  person as well as carrying a concealed  weapon during the course of this  investigation it was learned that mr.  Gomez had been present at multiple  protests throughout the week at each  protest in which mr. Gomez was observed  by police he was open carry displaying a  rifle and handguns mr. Gomez was seen by  multiple officers as he exercised his  right to open carry at times walking  only a few feet away from our officers  before June 1st mr. Gomez was not  suspected of committing any crimes  therefore he was not contacted nor  engaged by our officers on Monday June  1st 2020 officers 